{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 5, "model_name": "mistralai/mistral-small-4-119b-2603", "content": "Lo and behold good traveler mine here doth lie thy grand design for thy sojourn in Nippon’s fair and storied lands.\n\n**Day the First: The Rising Sun’s Embrace**\n\nUpon the morrow thou shalt alight in the bustling port of Narita or Kansai’s gate. Let not weariness stay thy steps but forthwith take thee to the city of Tokyo. There shall thou wander through the neon-lit streets of Shibuya where youth doth dance like revelers at fairy revels. Seek the ancient shrine of Meiji nestled in the forest’s heart where prayers whispered echo through the cedars.\n\n**Day the Second: The Floating World’s Whispers**\n\nWith the break of day set forth upon the Tokaido Shinkansen swift as Pegasus’ flight. Alight in Kyoto the erstwhile capital where emperors did hold court. Spend thy daylight hours in the hallowed halls of Kinkaku-ji where the golden pavilion gleams like the sun caught in a thousand mirrors. In the evening stroll through Gion’s lanes where geisha glide like specters of old and the scent of cherry blossoms lingers in the air.\n\n**Day the Third: The Dragon’s Lair**\n\nJourney onward to the mist-shrouded peaks of Hakone. There bathe thy bones in the healing waters of an onsen while gazing upon Fuji’s majesty as she slumbers behind veils of cloud. Let the steam of the bath carry thy cares away as the waters cleanse both body and soul.\n\n**Day the Fourth: The Way of the Samurai**\n\nTurn thy face westward to Hiroshima’s hallowed ground. Visit the Peace Memorial Park where the shadows of the past still linger and the river’s flow doth whisper of sorrow turned to hope. In the evening partake of the bounteous feast known as okonomiyaki that thy belly may be filled and thy spirit warmed.\n\n**Day the Fifth: The Land of the Gods**\n\nNorthward bound to the sacred isle of Miyajima. There in the waters stands the torii gate of Itsukushima grand as the gates of Olympus. Walk the island’s paths and gaze upon the deer that roam as though they were lords of the realm. As the sun dips low witness the gate’s reflection upon the tide a sight to stir even the stoniest heart.\n\n**Day the Sixth: The Merchant’s Dance**\n\nReturn to Osaka the kitchen of the nation where thou shalt feast upon takoyaki and okonomiyaki until thy doublet bursts at the seams. Climb the great castle of Osaka where the ghosts of past battles still murmur in the evening breeze. Let thy voice join the throngs in song at Dotonbori where the signs do leer like jesters in a play.\n\n**Day the Seventh: The Parting Guest**\n\nWith a heavy heart turn thy steps toward Narita or Kansai once more. As thou dost board the plane let thy mind’s eye linger upon the lands thou hast traversed and the memories thou hast woven. Fare thee well traveler and may fortune’s favor ever be thine as thou departest from Nippon’s fair shores.\n\nThus endeth thy journey’s tale in seven acts as the seven heavens decree.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Lo", "logprob": -1.4606726169586182}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -2.0401484966278076}, {"token": " beh", "logprob": -0.4904385209083557}, {"token": "old", "logprob": -1.0847986231965479e-05}, {"token": " good", "logprob": -0.9263961315155029}, {"token": " travel", "logprob": -0.6851527690887451}, {"token": "er", "logprob": -6.198863957251888e-06}, {"token": " mine", "logprob": -0.8568261861801147}, {"token": " here", "logprob": -1.8193291425704956}, {"token": " d", "logprob": -1.610326886177063}, {"token": "oth", "logprob": -1.9073468138230965e-06}, {"token": " lie", "logprob": -0.8748383522033691}, {"token": " thy", "logprob": -0.2000623643398285}, {"token": " grand", "logprob": -1.058690071105957}, {"token": " design", "logprob": -0.9201803207397461}, {"token": " for", "logprob": -0.17977721989154816}, {"token": " thy", "logprob": -1.5621964931488037}, {"token": " so", "logprob": -1.0697040557861328}, {"token": "journ", "logprob": -7